  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-06-09T21:09:04.998Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It is great that users retain copyright on our original works and that you don't step in to take it from us the moment it is uploaded to VRChat.\n\nBut, according to the Terms of Service you do gain a license to the content that is perpetual and all encompassing. I would like to lobby for an update to the Terms of Service that ends this license (wherever possible) when content is removed from the service.\n\nHere is a comparison of a few different TOS documents from different social VR platforms:\ngoo.gl/eIW2sA\n\nYou will notice a few of them do have this in their terms, including Second Life who has been around for ages, so it seems to be legally reasonable and doable to have this provision in there.\n\nThank you for considering this!\n\n-OwlBoy",
